{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13626-the-children-of-two-demons","id":13626,"title":"The Children of Two Demons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-18T14:40:11-08:00","id":13626,"title":"The Children of Two Demons","content":"The book is joyfully ambiguous with the nature of a child between two demons. We know that children of Humans and Demons themselves can use Embeds, and we know that the Children of a Demon and a Demon has always been eradicated by overwhelming force by the Godmachine.<br /> <br /> So what do you think is the nature of such children? Say your a storyteller and you had to introduce on into your game what direction would you go with?<br /> <br /> <br /> I personally like the idea that these children can become baby Godmachines, or maybe just baby Gods period. The book even mentions that maybe all Angels are baby Godmachines, just that the Godmachine's method of keeping them in check have prevented them from growing to rival him.<br /> <br /> I also like the idea that maybe famous people from myth or history may have been the Children of two Demons.<br /> <br /> <br /> I get the feeling with how open ended this was left in the book, a feature not a bug in my opinion, that many will just say you shouldn't use this in your game, or no no no the God Machine would never allow it, but please lets not thread crap. This is a discussion on what would happen if one of these beings were born.<br /> <br /> Hell since we aren't given any special conditions on making them besides the &quot;natural way&quot; I don't see why we can't discuss what happens if you get twins or triplets, or any other multiple birth Scenarios.<br /> <br /> <br /> And in all the World of Darkness what do you think is the safest place from the Godmachine? Which supernaturals could protect you the best?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking two options as the best options.<br /> <br /> Option one being a Changeling Freehold. Find a strong Freehold and bargain for a pledge to deliver and raise a child in a guarded Hallow. After all some have pointed out that the Hedge seems the opposite of the Godmachine, and Perhaps Fae are Demons who Found Hell. Or maybe the First Fae are the Children of two Demons, and the Nature of Contracts is similar to Embeds. Embeds are built into the world to be Exploited, maybe these Demonspawn are like Next Gen Systems in that they don't have to rely on Embeds, they can forge Contracts with the System of the Universe instead.<br /> <br /> Option two I think are Mummys. A group of mummies are quite insanely powerful, even a match for angels, and their cults are well quite useful. If you somehow could seek protection from a group of Mummies its hard to imagine a more well established set of Guardians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T15:00:03-08:00","id":13637,"title":"","content":"Since the God-Machine (or at least its angels) has limited access to/influence over other realms than the physical one (and Twilight), putting the child in, say, the Hedge or even Arcadia, would probably be the safest.<br /> <br /> What I'm mostly curious about is how the God-Machine manages to *find* these demon children, when the demons themselves seem to elude the hunter-angels under normal circumstances (unless they break Cover, of course). Perhaps something related to the reason they are so forbidden acts as a beacon to which the God-Machine is drawn. And perhaps... Given the mechanical logic the God-Machine works under, perhaps this instant knowledge of where the child is located <i>is exactly</i> the reason these children are not allowed to live. Maybe they are in no way more special or powerful than any other demon, but they just happen to also emit a signal so loud and so intense that the God-Machine cannot ignore their presence and always opts for destruction as the quickest way to deal with the unknown factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","name":"sikker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T15:07:03-08:00","id":13646,"title":"","content":"Well one of the possibilities is the Next Gen Demons are born without Cover, combined with the fact that the Godmachine super doesn't want them around has resulted in the giant overwhelming suppression wave against the childrenz.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T16:44:36-08:00","id":13689,"title":"","content":"I'm already toying with the idea of having two demons going to Inferno in search after a &quot;safe place&quot; to give birth to a child and wait for him to grow up- which is going to make the child a true &quot;demon from Hell&quot;.<br /> <br /> About why the GM kills such babies, I think that even if the child is &quot;simply a demon/ angel&quot; it's enough for investing many efforts to kill him. After all, the GM has a monopoly over the creation of angels and it needs them for its missions. I don't see why it risk its monopoly by allowing demons to procreate independently- especially since the children would be free from its control. Its nothing personal- its just business..<br /> <br /> (either that, or that those children have some &quot;access&quot; to the GM, making them into &quot;programers&quot; which could freely &quot;hack&quot; its systems and control it. Or that it would result in angel which are similar from the Testament of Marco. That could work for those who want some more &quot;exotic&quot; explanation)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 11-18-2013, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T22:13:37-08:00","id":13792,"title":"","content":"What if the child of two demons isn't a Demon, but is rather a proto-<i>qashmal</i>? Think about it: Demon-Babies wouldn't need Infrastructure. They'd have access to insane power from the get-go, they'd probably have weird-looking forms (if they're born without Covers, who's to say they don't look like a hybrid of their parents' demon forms), and they aren't born beholden to the God-Machine, but more likely in opposition to it. Add to that that they're already <i>at least</i> running on Waste Heat, and maybe their metaphysical insides transform their inner power source into running on the far-removed-from-the-&quot;normal&quot;-power-sources Pyros.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T02:25:18-08:00","id":13884,"title":"","content":"My take on it? The messiah from the movie Legion (2010).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T03:42:13-08:00","id":13914,"title":"","content":"I really wonder, though, what it's like to be a child of two Demons.<br /> Nor Angel was ever born; they were created, and started out their life as mature adults, with all the knowledge and control over their powers they need. There's no such thing as an Angel child. An Angel hardly needs to learn anything to function and survive.<br /> Same goes for Demons. They do have a lot to learn, but it's more akin to a lone stranger in a foreign land, trying to figure out customs and culture and not to attract attention needlessly.<br /> So, what's up with a Demon child that is born? Do they start out knowing everything they need, just as their parents? Or do they need to learn the basics? How to walk, talk, discern mundane acts from Embeds and Exploits, stay under Cover? How can you even teach all those things, when no one of your own kind had to learn these in the first place? If maturity is not a quality they possess from the beginning, how can you convince them not to abuse their powers or rush to fight the GM? How do you teach morality to such a being, when you don't have to worry about it yourself? Do you even teach them basic morality? How is their Cover affected by a lack of morality? Do you get Dexter, only demonic?<br /> That must be fascinating. And terribly dangerous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T05:36:48-08:00","id":13947,"title":"","content":"Do note that we're cutting the &quot;G-M kills babies&quot; bit from the book. The question of what happens when two Unchained have a kid might get some follow-up, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T06:02:16-08:00","id":13963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13626-the-children-of-two-demons?p=13947#post13947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do note that we're cutting the &quot;G-M kills babies&quot; bit from the book. The question of what happens when two Unchained have a kid might get some follow-up, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty significant. I mean, I can understand that CCP Legal might not want to get behind &quot;Game: The Babykilling&quot;, but it was a pretty significant setting element in my opinion, so I'm curious what will replace it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","name":"sikker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T06:10:31-08:00","id":13966,"title":"","content":"Nothing, in the core book. <br /> <br /> And it's nothing to do with legal. We've put some pretty heinous stuff in books (hell, I had some yo-yo trying to say that my chapter in <b>Immortals</b> could only have been written by someone educated in forensics, which was a surprise to me, as I have no such education). It's just that RPGs have a long history of &quot;killing the doomspawn,&quot; it's a tired trope, and I think we can do better, given some time to develop it. But it's not a significant enough portion of the game to go screwing with pagination at this point, not when we've got an ST's Guide coming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T10:38:49-08:00","id":14159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13626-the-children-of-two-demons?p=13966#post13966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing, in the core book.<br /> <br /> And it's nothing to do with legal. We've put some pretty heinous stuff in books (hell, I had some yo-yo trying to say that my chapter in <b>Immortals</b> could only have been written by someone educated in forensics, which was a surprise to me, as I have no such education). It's just that RPGs have a long history of &quot;killing the doomspawn,&quot; it's a tired trope, and I think we can do better, given some time to develop it. But it's not a significant enough portion of the game to go screwing with pagination at this point, not when we've got an ST's Guide coming.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, CCP would've been fine with us doing this.<br /> <br /> Matt's covered the taste and cliche issue. I also want to explore some related questions in later books, and blocking off the whole subject in one sidebar felt like overkill. Plus, with the directions I'm thinking we could take heirs to hell, they wouldn't logically be an overwhelming nuke-it-from-orbit priority for the God-Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T13:35:56-08:00","id":14260,"title":"","content":"Could you keep the info that a Cover can have kids, though?<br /> <br /> I don't want having to answer the &quot;Can a demon have kids?&quot; question when we already know. Besides, a true half-demon seems like an interesting hook in and of itself, leaving pure demon-child out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T14:01:14-08:00","id":14269,"title":"","content":"Where I to touch on it in a Demon game I'd brown note it. Have the child be born and the GM going haywire to stop it. Have PCs running interference. Hiding it in another realm wouldn't go terribly well... it'd just shift the antagonists. Hide it in the Hedge? Fae. Hide it in the underworld? Deathlords. Etc etc.<br /> <br /> That said, as the devs have said. Its sort of been done before and is highly formulaic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T14:04:39-08:00","id":14275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13626-the-children-of-two-demons?p=14260#post14260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you keep the info that a Cover can have kids, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think they ever said they were planning on cutting the entire sidebar. Just that one portion of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T14:48:59-08:00","id":14307,"title":"","content":"I'm glad you're ditching it. It was dreadfully cliche and more in line with Earlier products that were carefully conservative about this type of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T17:09:15-08:00","id":14980,"title":"","content":"I must admit, I was immediately reminded of Werewolf doomchildren.<br /> <br /> But it's so cool and mysterious! Please, insert something else the G-M inexplicably panics over, it's really very thematic. *puppydog eyes*<br /> <br /> My two cents, ignoring the fact that this will be expunged from canon: they would actually have free will, and thus *not* be pawns of the God-Machine. Y'know, unlike regular Demons:]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}